  "description": "The proposed works involve the retrofitting of existing single-glazed timber sash windows with high-quality, double-glazed sash units, utilising slim-profile glazing to maintain the traditional appearance. The new sashes will be constructed in sustainably sourced hardwood and installed within the existing, original timber window frames, which are to be carefully retained and refurbished where necessary.\n\nAll new sashes will precisely replicate the existing historic detailing, including the glazing bar pattern, sash horns, dimensions, and depth of recess. The windows will be painted in white to match the current colour and finish, ensuring continuity with the property's original aesthetic. The aim of the works is to improve thermal efficiency and reduce energy loss while fully preserving the architectural integrity and historic character of the building within the Ladywell Conservation Area.\n\nNo alterations are proposed to the openings, external masonry, or visual proportions of the windows. The works are entirely sympathetic in design, materials, and craftsmanship to the period character of the house and have been designed in accordance with Lewisham’s conservation guidelines and the Ladywell Conservation Area Appraisal.",
